<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!--
    One palette for three products — and it is NO LONGER HERE.

    Every colour this file used to declare now comes from `Common.Theme`, the shared library the
    mod and this tool both consume, and is posted into the application's resources by
    ThemeResources.Apply before the first window is built. The keys are unchanged, so every
    {DynamicResource} in this project still resolves exactly as it did.

    ⚠ Why it moved, because the reason matters more than the move (the full account is in
    ThemeResources and in Common.Theme):

      · the literals here were **Tailwind v3** while the website has moved to **v4**, whose palette
        was rebuilt in oklch. The tool written to look like the site had quietly drifted from it —
        purple-600 #9333EA against #9810FA, orange-500 #F97316 against #FF6900;
      · the surfaces had been sampled from a SCREENSHOT of the running site, where animated
        coloured blobs in the background lighten anything picked off them. That is why this window
        came out a shade paler than both the site and the mod;
      · and the previous comment in this file claimed the status colours were "shared by the site
        and the mod already". They were not. Checked line by line: the mod's were neighbours of
        these, never equal, and its quality bar disagreed on three bands out of five.

    ⚠ Do not put a colour back in here. Two copies of a palette is what produced all of the above,
    and the socle's check project now refuses a drift.

    What stays: shape. It is a XAML notion, no consumer of the library needs it, and there is
    nothing to keep in step.
  -->

  <!-- Shape — rounded-lg is the site's radius on cards, inputs and buttons alike -->
  <CornerRadius x:Key="RadiusCard">8</CornerRadius>
  <CornerRadius x:Key="RadiusControl">8</CornerRadius>

</ResourceDictionary>
